WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.344
Priya: Approve a deletion budget of ten objects. One tenant only, with scoped credentials restored.

2
00:00:07.344 --> 00:00:13.248
Lukas: Keep the stop switch within reach. An unexpected path is a rollback trigger.

3
00:00:13.248 --> 00:00:20.807
Raj: Just to confirm, stop means disable the scheduler, right? And terminate the active process group.

4
00:00:20.807 --> 00:00:28.487
Anika: Yes, revoke cleanup access if needed too. Existing consumer reads use their separate identity.

5
00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:37.823
Hannah: The deletion manifest matches approved candidates exactly. No shared artifact path appears in execution.

6
00:00:37.823 --> 00:00:45.167
Raj: Okay, actual removals stay below the budget. Rejected candidates remain untouched in this run.

7
00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:51.599
Lukas: Reads remain healthy through the canary. Let's keep it under observation before expansion.

8
00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:58.822
Priya: Maybe we'll expand tomorrow after another review. No automatic fleet-wide catch-up run tonight.

9
00:00:58.822 --> 00:01:07.006
Hannah: Record both denied and successful operations. We need evidence that the limits actually applied.

10
00:01:07.006 --> 00:01:14.470
Anika: Agreed, backups and recovery routing stay available. We'll retain the incident hold until closure.

